    {
      "id": "L1",
      "source_unit": "U6a",
      "text": "Platform-specific build workarounds (e.g. Windows EISDIR) in next.config.mjs must be guarded by platform and must not alter the Linux/Docker build path."
    },
    {
      "id": "L2",
      "source_unit": "U6d",
      "text": "Do not monkey-patch the `api` client object or `window.fetch` to observe responses. Cross-cutting behaviour such as 401 handling must be a hook inside the central request function in `api.ts`, registered by the consumer."
    },
    {
      "id": "L3",
      "source_unit": "U9",
      "text": "Documentation must be checked against the ADRs and the actual code. Do not state behaviours (password policy, audit fields, config fallbacks, command syntax) that were not verified. Shell commands in docs must be runnable as written."
    }
